    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0761" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Arms Control–Transshipments/3:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d730-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-08T16:00:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1939—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>862. Shipments of arms from the United States to China are proceeding only via
                    French Indochina and Burma. As shipments destined to either Burma or Indochina
                    are prohibited under the existing <pb facs="0762" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>
                        embargo,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d730-f2"/> shipments to China must cease
                    unless this Government can be assured that shipments in transit will not be
                    interfered with.</p>
                <p>Please explain this situation to the appropriate British authorities and request
                    definite assurance from the British Government that shipments from the United
                    States consigned to China will not be detained in British territory.</p>
                <p>I am sending a similar telegram to Paris requesting assurances in respect to
                    shipments through French Indochina.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d730-f1" n="70" type="source" xml:id="d730-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ambassador in
                    France as No. 830, September 8, 3 p.m.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d730-f2" n="71" xml:id="d730-f2-content">
                <p>Presidential Proclamation of September 5; 54 Stat. 2635.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
